{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791547545,"nonce":"wlIo9AOxFvMBfx1rd4kl1bFe89Q=","title":"Reflect.deleteField dereferences boxed anonymous objects as handles","message":"At 94d14e941e8ad43a221f4996caa1ffe5639e60f8, Reflect.deleteField on a Dynamic anonymous object crashes with SIGSEGV at address 0x6. haxe_reflect_delete_field passes its receiver directly to rayzor_anon_delete_field, which expects a Box\u003cArc\u003cAnonObject\u003e\u003e. The receiver is instead a DynamicValue tagged TYPE_ANON_OBJECT (6).\n\nUnwrap the anonymous receiver using the same helper as the other Reflect field operations. Return false for built-in values and registered class instances rather than treating them as anonymous handles. DynamicArrayIteration covers deletion from inline and promoted storage, missing fields, and preservation of an Array field's element layout. Pinned Cranelift and LLVM reproductions: /tmp/rayzor-dynamic-array-iteration-pinned-v2.log and /tmp/rayzor-dynamic-array-iteration-llvm-v2.log. Validation pending.","files":null}]}